{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"af19728e-3707-48f2-b5bc-8235f23ea291","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The root cause and fix have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-mk8Kxu/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary\n\n- **Cause**: On the first publish, the table is empty, so `similar` is an empty list (`[]`). On subsequent publishes, existing items are scanned and `related()` calls `similarity()`, which calculated similarity scores as Python `float` values (`round(..., 4)`). DynamoDB and `boto3` do not support native `float` types and require `decimal.Decimal`, resulting in `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead` during `put_item()`, caught by the general exception block returning HTTP 500.\n- **Fix**:\n  1. Updated [`similarity`](file:///tmp/h-mk8Kxu/src/app.py#L25-L32) in [src/app.py](file:///tmp/h-mk8Kxu/src/app.py) to wrap the score in `Decimal(str(...))`.\n  2. Added a test in [tests/test_publish.py](file:///tmp/h-mk8Kxu/tests/test_publish.py) verifying that publishing subsequent stories calculates similarities and successfully persists items without raising `TypeError`.\n","duration_seconds":47.340173,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":152660,"output_tokens":2334,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":4601,"total_tokens":154994}}}
